  26:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  27:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   ==============================================================================
  28:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
  29:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     This driver implements a high level communication layer for read and write from/to
  30:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     this memory. The needed STM32 hardware resources (SDMMC and GPIO) are performed by
ARM GAS  /var/tmp//ccIYEkVU.s 			page 2


  31:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     the user in HAL_SD_MspInit() function (MSP layer).
  32:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Basically, the MSP layer configuration should be the same as we provide in the
  33:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     examples.
  34:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     You can easily tailor this configuration according to hardware resources.
  35:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  36:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
  37:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     This driver is a generic layered driver for SDMMC memories which uses the HAL
  38:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     SDMMC driver functions to interface with SD and uSD cards devices.
  39:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     It is used as follows:
  40:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  41:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#)Initialize the SDMMC low level resources by implementing the HAL_SD_MspInit() API:
  42:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) Call the function HAL_RCCEx_PeriphCLKConfig with RCC_PERIPHCLK_SDMMC1 for
  43:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         PeriphClockSelection and select SDMMC1 clock source (MSI, main PLL or PLLSAI1)
  44:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) Enable the SDMMC interface clock using __HAL_RCC_SDMMC1_CLK_ENABLE();
  45:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) SDMMC pins configuration for SD card
  46:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Enable the clock for the SDMMC GPIOs using the functions __HAL_RCC_GPIOx_CLK_ENAB
  47:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Configure these SDMMC pins as alternate function pull-up using HAL_GPIO_Init()
  48:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and according to your pin assignment;
  49:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) On STM32L4Rx/STM32L4Sxx devices, no DMA configuration is need, an internal DMA for SDM
  50:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) On other devices, perform DMA configuration if you need to use DMA process (HAL_SD_Rea
  51:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****              and HAL_SD_WriteBlocks_DMA() APIs).
  52:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Enable the DMAx interface clock using __HAL_RCC_DMAx_CLK_ENABLE();
  53:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Configure the DMA using the function HAL_DMA_Init() with predeclared and filled.
  54:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process when using DMA transfer.
  55:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Configure the SDMMC and DMA interrupt priorities using functions
  56:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   HAL_NVIC_SetPriority(); DMA priority is superior to SDMMC's priority
  57:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Enable the NVIC DMA and SDMMC IRQs using function HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ()
  58:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) SDMMC interrupts are managed using the macros __HAL_SD_ENABLE_IT()
  59:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and __HAL_SD_DISABLE_IT() inside the communication process.
  60:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) SDMMC interrupts pending bits are managed using the macros __HAL_SD_GET_IT()
  61:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and __HAL_SD_CLEAR_IT()
  62:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process (HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_IT()
  63:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****              and HAL_SD_WriteBlocks_IT() APIs).
  64:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Configure the SDMMC interrupt priorities using function HAL_NVIC_SetPriority();
  65:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Enable the NVIC SDMMC IRQs using function HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ()
  66:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) SDMMC interrupts are managed using the macros __HAL_SD_ENABLE_IT()
  67:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and __HAL_SD_DISABLE_IT() inside the communication process.
  68:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) SDMMC interrupts pending bits are managed using the macros __HAL_SD_GET_IT()
  69:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and __HAL_SD_CLEAR_IT()
  70:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) At this stage, you can perform SD read/write/erase operations after SD card initialization
  71:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  72:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  73:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   *** SD Card Initialization and configuration ***
  74:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   ================================================
  75:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
  76:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     To initialize the SD Card, use the HAL_SD_Init() function. It Initializes
  77:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     SDMMC Peripheral(STM32 side) and the SD Card, and put it into StandBy State (Ready for data tra
  78:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     This function provide the following operations:
  79:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  80:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Apply the SD Card initialization process at 400KHz and check the SD Card
  81:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         type (Standard Capacity or High Capacity). You can change or adapt this
  82:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         frequency by adjusting the "ClockDiv" field.
  83:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         The SD Card frequency (SDMMC_CK) is computed as follows:
  84:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  85:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****            SDMMC_CK = SDMMCCLK / (2 * ClockDiv) on STM32L4Rx/STM32L4Sxx devices
  86:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****            SDMMC_CK = SDMMCCLK / (ClockDiv + 2) on other devices
  87:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
ARM GAS  /var/tmp//ccIYEkVU.s 			page 3


  88:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         In initialization mode and according to the SD Card standard,
  89:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         make sure that the SDMMC_CK frequency doesn't exceed 400KHz.
  90:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  91:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This phase of initialization is done through SDMMC_Init() and
  92:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         SDMMC_PowerState_ON() SDMMC low level APIs.
  93:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  94:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Initialize the SD card. The API used is HAL_SD_InitCard().
  95:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This phase allows the card initialization and identification
  96:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         and check the SD Card type (Standard Capacity or High Capacity)
  97:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         The initialization flow is compatible with SD standard.
  98:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  99:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This API (HAL_SD_InitCard()) could be used also to reinitialize the card in case
 100:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         of plug-off plug-in.
 101:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 102:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Configure the SD Card Data transfer frequency. You can change or adapt this
 103:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         frequency by adjusting the "ClockDiv" field.
 104:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         In transfer mode and according to the SD Card standard, make sure that the
 105:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         SDMMC_CK frequency doesn't exceed 25MHz and 100MHz in High-speed mode switch.
 106:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 107:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Select the corresponding SD Card according to the address read with the step 2.
 108:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 109:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Configure the SD Card in wide bus mode: 4-bits data.
 110:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 111:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   *** SD Card Read operation ***
 112:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   ==============================
 113:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
 114:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in polling mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks().
 115:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 116:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 117:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 118:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 119:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 120:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 121:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 122:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in DMA mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_DMA().
 123:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 124:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 125:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 126:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 127:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 128:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 129:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You could also check the DMA transfer process through the SD Rx interrupt event.
 130:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 131:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in Interrupt mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_IT().
 132:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 133:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 134:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 135:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 136:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 137:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 138:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****         You could also check the IT transfer process through the SD Rx interrupt event.
 139:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
