 208:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   *** Callback registration ***
 209:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   =============================================
 210:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
 211:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     The compilation define USE_HAL_SD_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 212:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 213:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 214:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Use Functions HAL_SD_RegisterCallback() to register a user callback,
 215:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     it allows to register following callbacks:
 216:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) TxCpltCallback : callback when a transmission transfer is completed.
 217:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) RxCpltCallback : callback when a reception transfer is completed.
 218:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) ErrorCallback : callback when error occurs.
 219:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) AbortCpltCallback : callback when abort is completed.
 220:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Read_DMADblBuf0CpltCallback : callback when the DMA reception of first buffer is complete
 221:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Read_DMADblBuf1CpltCallback : callback when the DMA reception of second buffer is complet
 222:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Write_DMADblBuf0CpltCallback : callback when the DMA transmission of first buffer is comp
 223:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Write_DMADblBuf1CpltCallback : callback when the DMA transmission of second buffer is com
 224:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : SD MspInit.
 225:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : SD MspDeInit.
 226:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 227:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     and a pointer to the user callback function.
 228:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     For specific callbacks TransceiverCallback use dedicated register callbacks:
 229:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     respectively HAL_SD_RegisterTransceiverCallback().
 230:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 231:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Use function HAL_SD_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 232:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     weak (surcharged) function. It allows to reset following callbacks:
 233:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) TxCpltCallback : callback when a transmission transfer is completed.
 234:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) RxCpltCallback : callback when a reception transfer is completed.
 235:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) ErrorCallback : callback when error occurs.
 236:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) AbortCpltCallback : callback when abort is completed.
 237:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Read_DMADblBuf0CpltCallback : callback when the DMA reception of first buffer is complete
 238:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Read_DMADblBuf1CpltCallback : callback when the DMA reception of second buffer is complet
 239:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Write_DMADblBuf0CpltCallback : callback when the DMA transmission of first buffer is comp
 240:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Write_DMADblBuf1CpltCallback : callback when the DMA transmission of second buffer is com
 241:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : SD MspInit.
 242:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : SD MspDeInit.
 243:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     This function) takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle and the Callback ID.
 244:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     For specific callbacks TransceiverCallback use dedicated unregister callbacks:
 245:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     respectively HAL_SD_UnRegisterTransceiverCallback().
 246:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 247:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     By default, after the HAL_SD_Init and if the state is HAL_SD_STATE_RESET
 248:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     all callbacks are reset to the corresponding legacy weak (surcharged) functions.
 249:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit callbacks that are respectively
 250:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     reset to the legacy weak (surcharged) functions in the HAL_SD_Init
 251:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     and HAL_SD_DeInit only when these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 252:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_SD_Init and HAL_SD_DeInit
 253:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand)
 254:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 255:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in READY state only.
 256:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     Exception done for MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks that can be registered/unregistered
 257:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     in READY or RESET state, thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used
 258:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     during the Init/DeInit.
ARM GAS  /var/tmp//ccIYEkVU.s 			page 6


 259:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 260:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     using HAL_SD_RegisterCallback before calling HAL_SD_DeInit
 261:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     or HAL_SD_Init function.
 262:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 263:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     When The compilation define USE_HAL_SD_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 264:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     not defined, the callback registering feature is not available
 265:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c ****     and weak (surcharged) callbacks are used.
 266:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_sd.c **** 
